IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`

-- sga-parts8-9.l4: Parts 8 and 9 (sections 63A to 80) of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Commonwealth),
-- Federal Register compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion (not the authorised text).
-- Part 8: payments of shortfall components for the benefit of employees. Part 9: partnerships, associations, the amnesty, records, regulations.
-- Section 80 (regulations) is machinery and is encoded only for the limit it puts on the penalty regulations may prescribe; NOTES.md says so.
-- The value of a penalty unit is in section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, which is not among the sources: it is a plain input.

§ `Section 63A: payments to which Part 8 applies`

-- src:1169 | (1) This Part applies to a charge payment in respect of one or more employees (the benefiting employee or benefiting employees) that is made by or on behalf of an employer.
@ref s 63A(1), (1A), (2) (src:1169-1169)
-- src:1170 | (1A) This Part applies to a former employee as if the former employee were an employee of the person who was the former employee’s employer.
@ref s 63A(1), (1A), (2) (src:1170-1170)
-- src:1171 | (2) In this section:
-- src:1172 | charge payment means a payment of superannuation guarantee charge that:
-- src:1173 | (a) was assessed in relation to a QE day; or
-- src:1174 | (b) was in the form of general interest charge payable under section 49 in relation to non-payment of superannuation guarantee charge assessed in relation to a QE day.
-- src:1175 | Estimates under the Taxation Administration Act 1953
@ref s 63A(1), (1A), (2) (src:1171-1175)
GIVEN `the payment was assessed in relation to a QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment was in the form of general interest charge payable under section 49 in relation to non-payment of charge assessed in relation to a QE day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by or on behalf of an employer in respect of one or more employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Part 8 applies to the payment` MEANS
    `it is made by or on behalf of an employer in respect of one or more employees`
    AND (`the payment was assessed in relation to a QE day` OR `the payment was in the form of general interest charge payable under section 49 in relation to non-payment of charge assessed in relation to a QE day`)

-- 63A(3), (4): an amount paid to the Commonwealth is treated as a payment of charge to the extent a liability is discharged under the Taxation Administration Act 1953; not until the Commissioner knows which employees the liability was in respect of.
-- src:1176 | (3) For the purposes of this Part, an amount paid to the Commonwealth is treated as being a payment of superannuation guarantee charge:
-- src:1177 | (a) in respect of an employee or employees; and
-- src:1178 | (b) made by or on behalf of an employer;
-- src:1179 | to the extent that, as a result of the amount being paid to the Commonwealth, a liability of the employer to pay superannuation guarantee charge in respect of that employee or those employees is discharged under subsection 268-20(3), or section 269-40, in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
-- src:1180 | Note: Under Division 268 in that Schedule, the Commissioner may make an estimate of the unpaid and overdue amount of an employer’s superannuation guarantee charge for a QE day.
@ref s 63A(3), (4) (src:1176-1180)
-- src:1181 | (4) However, subsection (3) does not apply to the amount until the Commissioner knows which employee or employees the liability to pay the superannuation guarantee charge was in respect of.
@ref s 63A(3), (4) (src:1181-1181)
GIVEN `the amount by which a liability to pay charge is discharged under subsection 268-20(3), or section 269-40, in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner knows which employee or employees the liability was in respect of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount treated as a payment of superannuation guarantee charge for Part 8` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner knows which employee or employees the liability was in respect of` THEN JUST `the amount by which a liability to pay charge is discharged under subsection 268-20(3), or section 269-40, in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953` ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1183 | (1) If a payment to which this Part applies is made, the Commissioner is required to pay (or otherwise deal with) an amount, which is called the shortfall component, for the benefit of a benefiting employee under sections 65 to 67.
@ref s 63B(1) (src:1183-1183)
GIVEN `Part 8 applies to the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner is required to pay or deal with the shortfall component for the benefit of a benefiting employee` MEANS
    IF `Part 8 applies to the payment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 64A and 64B: the shortfall component`

-- 64A(3): the employee entitlement is the sum of (a) the individual final shortfall, (b) the notional earnings component, (c) the choice loading, (d) the general interest charge on those that has been paid or is payable at the time, less previous payments, but not below zero.
-- src:1191 | (3) The employee entitlement, calculated at a particular time in relation to the assessment, is the sum of the following amounts:
-- src:1192 | (a) the employer’s individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall for the employee and the QE day specified in the assessment;
-- src:1193 | (b) the employer’s individual notional earnings component for the employee and the QE day;
-- src:1194 | (c) the employer’s choice loading for the employee and the QE day;
-- src:1195 | (d) so much of any general interest charge as:
-- src:1196 | (i) relates to non-payment of superannuation guarantee charge payable in relation to the amounts in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c); and
-- src:1197 | (ii) has been paid by, or is payable at, the particular time;
-- src:1198 | reduced (but not below zero) by the amounts of any previous payments to which this Part applies that relate to the QE day, employer and employee.
-- src:1199 | Note: The employee’s entitlement does not include so much of any general interest charge as relates to the employer’s administrative uplift amount for the QE day (see subparagraph (d)(i)).
@ref s 64A(3) (src:1191-1199)
GIVEN `the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual notional earnings component` IS A NUMBER
      `the choice loading` IS A NUMBER
      `the general interest charge on those amounts paid or payable at the time` IS A NUMBER
      `the previous payments to which this Part applies that relate to the QE day, employer and employee` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the employee entitlement` MEANS
    IF previous GREATER THAN sum THEN 0 ELSE sum MINUS previous
    WHERE
        sum MEANS (`the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfall` PLUS `the individual notional earnings component`) PLUS (`the choice loading` PLUS `the general interest charge on those amounts paid or payable at the time`)
        previous MEANS `the previous payments to which this Part applies that relate to the QE day, employer and employee`

-- src:1187 | (1) This section applies if there is only one benefiting employee.
@ref s 64A(1), (2) (src:1187-1187)
-- src:1188 | (2) The shortfall component for the payment is the lesser of the following amounts:
-- src:1189 | (a) the amount of the payment;
-- src:1190 | (b) the amount of the employee entitlement, calculated at the time when the payment is made (see subsection (3)).
@ref s 64A(1), (2) (src:1188-1190)
GIVEN `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee entitlement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shortfall component for one benefiting employee` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the payment` AT MOST `the employee entitlement` THEN `the amount of the payment` ELSE `the employee entitlement`

-- src:1209 | (4) The total employee entitlement, calculated at a particular time in relation to the assessment, is the sum of the following amounts:
-- src:1210 | (a) the total of the employer’s individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for all employees and the QE day specified in the assessment;
-- src:1211 | (b) the total of the employer’s individual notional earnings components for all employees and the QE day;
-- src:1212 | (c) the total of the employer’s choice loadings for all employees and the QE day;
-- src:1213 | (d) so much of any general interest charge as:
-- src:1214 | (i) relates to non-payment of superannuation guarantee charge payable in relation to the totals in paragraphs (a), (b) and (c); and
-- src:1215 | (ii) has been paid by, or is payable at, the particular time;
-- src:1216 | reduced (but not below zero) by the amounts of any previous payments to which this Part applies that relate to the QE day, employer and employees.
-- src:1217 | Note: The employee’s entitlement does not include so much of any general interest charge as relates to the employer’s administrative uplift amount for the QE day (see subparagraph (d)(i)).
@ref s 64B(4) (src:1209-1217)
GIVEN `the total of the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for all employees` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the individual notional earnings components for all employees` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the choice loadings for all employees` IS A NUMBER
      `the general interest charge on those totals paid or payable at the time` IS A NUMBER
      `the previous payments to which this Part applies that relate to the QE day, employer and employees` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total employee entitlement` MEANS
    IF previous GREATER THAN sum THEN 0 ELSE sum MINUS previous
    WHERE
        sum MEANS (`the total of the individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for all employees` PLUS `the total of the individual notional earnings components for all employees`) PLUS (`the total of the choice loadings for all employees` PLUS `the general interest charge on those totals paid or payable at the time`)
        previous MEANS `the previous payments to which this Part applies that relate to the QE day, employer and employees`

-- 64B(3): an employee's proportion is (the employee's final shortfall, notional earnings component and choice loading) / (the total of those for all employees); 64B(3A): the Commissioner may vary it.
-- src:1205 | (3) Subject to subsection (3A), an employee’s proportion of an amount is the following proportion:
@ref s 64B(3), (3A) (src:1205-1205)
-- src:1206 | (3A) The Commissioner may vary an employee’s proportion of an amount if the amount of the charge payment has been affected by:
-- src:1207 | (a) the application of the monetary limit imposed by subsection 556(1A) of the Corporations Act 2001 in respect of the employee; or
-- src:1208 | (b) the application of the monetary limit imposed by paragraph 109(1)(e) of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 in respect of the employee.
@ref s 64B(3), (3A) (src:1206-1208)
GIVEN `the total of the individual final shortfall, individual notional earnings component and choice loading for the employee` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the individual final shortfalls, individual notional earnings components and choice loadings for all employees` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion the Commissioner varies it to, if the charge payment was affected by a monetary limit in section 556(1A) of the Corporations Act 2001 or paragraph 109(1)(e) of the Bankruptcy Act 1966` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`an employee's proportion of an amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the proportion the Commissioner varies it to, if the charge payment was affected by a monetary limit in section 556(1A) of the Corporations Act 2001 or paragraph 109(1)(e) of the Bankruptcy Act 1966`
    WHEN JUST varied THEN JUST varied
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the total of the individual final shortfalls, individual notional earnings components and choice loadings for all employees` EQUALS 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (`the total of the individual final shortfall, individual notional earnings component and choice loading for the employee` DIVIDED BY `the total of the individual final shortfalls, individual notional earnings components and choice loadings for all employees`)

-- src:1201 | (1) This section applies if there is more than one benefiting employee. In this situation, separate shortfall components are worked out for each of the benefiting employees.
@ref s 64B(1), (2) (src:1201-1201)
-- src:1202 | (2) The shortfall component for a payment, in respect of a particular employee, is the employee’s proportion of the lesser of the following amounts:
-- src:1203 | (a) the amount of the payment;
-- src:1204 | (b) the amount of the total employee entitlement, calculated at the time when the payment is made.
@ref s 64B(1), (2) (src:1202-1204)
GIVEN `the amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the total employee entitlement` IS A NUMBER
      proportion IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shortfall component for a payment in respect of a particular employee` MEANS
    proportion TIMES (IF `the amount of the payment` AT MOST `the total employee entitlement` THEN `the amount of the payment` ELSE `the total employee entitlement`)

§ `Sections 65 to 67: dealing with the shortfall component`

-- src:1219 | (1) Except in a case covered by section 65AA, 65A, 66, 66A or 67, the Commissioner is required to deal with the amount of the shortfall component in one of the following ways:
-- src:1220 | (a) in any case—pay the amount of the component, for the benefit of the employee, to:
-- src:1221 | (i) an RSA; or
-- src:1222 | (ii) an account with a complying superannuation fund; or
-- src:1223 | (iii) an account with a complying approved deposit fund;
-- src:1224 | that is held in the name of the employee and that is determined by the Commissioner to belong to the employee;
-- src:1225 | (b) if the employee has nominated an RSA, a complying superannuation fund or a complying approved deposit fund in accordance with the regulations:
-- src:1226 | (i) pay the amount of the component to the RSA or fund for the benefit of the employee; or
-- src:1227 | (ii) make arrangements in accordance with the regulations to enable the amount of the component to be paid to the RSA or fund for the benefit of the employee;
-- src:1228 | (c) if the employee has not made a nomination under paragraph (b)—credit the amount of the component to an account kept under the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995 in the name of the employee.
@ref s 65(1) (src:1219-1228)
GIVEN `section 65AA, 65A, 66, 66A or 67 covers the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has nominated an RSA, a complying superannuation fund or a complying approved deposit fund in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the ways the Commissioner may deal with the shortfall component under section 65(1)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 65AA, 65A, 66, 66A or 67 covers the case` THEN EMPTY
           IF `the employee has nominated an RSA, a complying superannuation fund or a complying approved deposit fund in accordance with the regulations`
              THEN LIST "pay it for the benefit of the employee to an RSA, or an account with a complying superannuation fund or complying approved deposit fund, held in the name of the employee and determined by the Commissioner to belong to the employee", "pay it to the nominated RSA or fund for the benefit of the employee", "make arrangements in accordance with the regulations to enable it to be paid to the nominated RSA or fund"
           OTHERWISE LIST "pay it for the benefit of the employee to an RSA, or an account with a complying superannuation fund or complying approved deposit fund, held in the name of the employee and determined by the Commissioner to belong to the employee", "credit it to an account kept under the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995 in the name of the employee"

-- src:1229 | (2) A payment of the amount of a shortfall component made or arranged by the Commissioner for the benefit of an employee to a superannuation fund is conclusively presumed to be a payment to a complying superannuation fund for the purposes of subsection (1) if, at the time the payment is made, the Commissioner has obtained a written statement, provided by or on behalf of the trustee of the fund, that the fund:
-- src:1230 | (a) is a resident regulated superannuation fund within the meaning of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993; and
-- src:1231 | (b) is not subject to a direction under section 63 of that Act.
@ref s 65(2), (3), (4) (src:1229-1231)
-- src:1232 | (3) A payment of the amount of a shortfall component made or arranged by the Commissioner for the benefit of an employee to an approved deposit fund is conclusively presumed to be a payment to a complying approved deposit fund for the purposes of subsection (1) if subsection (4) applies.
@ref s 65(2), (3), (4) (src:1232-1232)
-- src:1233 | (4) This subsection applies if, at the time the payment is made, the Commissioner has obtained a written statement, provided by or on behalf of the trustee of the fund, that the fund is operated in accordance with the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 and regulations under that Act.
@ref s 65(2), (3), (4) (src:1233-1233)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has obtained, at the time of the payment, a written statement by or for the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says the fund is a resident regulated superannuation fund and is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993, or (for an approved deposit fund) is operated in accordance with that Act and its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the payment is conclusively presumed to be a payment to a complying fund` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has obtained, at the time of the payment, a written statement by or for the trustee` AND `the statement says the fund is a resident regulated superannuation fund and is not subject to a direction under section 63 of the Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993, or (for an approved deposit fund) is operated in accordance with that Act and its regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1234 | (5) If an amount is to be credited under paragraph (1)(c), an amount equal to the credited amount is to be credited to the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account.
@ref s 65(5), (6) (src:1234-1234)
-- src:1235 | (6) A payment under paragraph (1)(a) to a particular account is taken to be a payment to the complying superannuation fund or the complying approved deposit fund with which the account is held, for the purposes of this section and any other laws of the Commonwealth that refer to payments under this section.
@ref s 65(5), (6) (src:1235-1235)
GIVEN `the amount credited under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount credited to the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account` MEANS `the amount credited under paragraph (1)(c)`

-- src:1236 | 65AA Shortfall component and former temporary resident
-- src:1237 | (1) This section applies if the employee is a former temporary resident (within the meaning of the Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999).
-- src:1238 | (2) The Commissioner must treat the amount of the shortfall component as if it had been paid to the Commissioner by a superannuation provider in respect of the employee under section 20F of that Act.
@ref s 65AA (src:1236-1238)
GIVEN `the employee is a former temporary resident within the meaning of the Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must treat the shortfall component as paid by a superannuation provider under section 20F of that Act` MEANS
    IF `the employee is a former temporary resident within the meaning of the Superannuation (Unclaimed Money and Lost Members) Act 1999` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1239 | 65A Payment to employee who is over 65
-- src:1240 | Except in a case covered by section 65AA, the Commissioner must pay the amount of the shortfall component directly to the employee (whether or not he or she is still an employee) if:
-- src:1241 | (a) the employee is 65 years or more; and
-- src:1242 | (b) the employee has requested the Commissioner in the approved form to pay the amount to him or her.
@ref s 65A (src:1239-1242)
GIVEN `section 65AA covers the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of the employee in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the employee has requested the Commissioner in the approved form to pay the amount to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must pay the shortfall component directly to an employee who is over 65` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 65AA covers the case` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the age of the employee in years` AT LEAST 65 AND `the employee has requested the Commissioner in the approved form to pay the amount to the employee` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1243 | 66 Payment to employee retired due to permanent incapacity or invalidity
-- src:1244 | Except in a case covered by section 65AA, if:
-- src:1245 | (a) the employee has retired because of permanent incapacity or permanent invalidity; and
-- src:1246 | (b) the former employee has lodged with the Commissioner:
-- src:1247 | (i) written notice of the retirement; and
-- src:1248 | (ii) a copy of a certificate signed by 2 registered medical practitioners certifying that the former employee is unlikely to be able to work again in a capacity for which he or she is reasonably qualified by education, training or experience;
-- src:1249 | the Commissioner must pay the amount of the shortfall component to the former employee.
@ref s 66 (src:1243-1249)
GIVEN `section 65AA covers the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has retired because of permanent incapacity or permanent invalidity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the former employee has lodged written notice of the retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of registered medical practitioners who signed the certificate that the former employee is unlikely to be able to work again in a capacity for which reasonably qualified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must pay the shortfall component to an employee retired due to permanent incapacity or invalidity` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 65AA covers the case` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the employee has retired because of permanent incapacity or permanent invalidity` AND `the former employee has lodged written notice of the retirement` AND `the number of registered medical practitioners who signed the certificate that the former employee is unlikely to be able to work again in a capacity for which reasonably qualified` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1250 | 66A Payment to employee with terminal medical condition
-- src:1251 | Except in a case covered by section 65AA, the Commissioner must pay the amount of the shortfall component to the employee (whether or not he or she is still an employee) if:
-- src:1252 | (a) a terminal medical condition (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997) exists in relation to the employee; and
-- src:1253 | (b) the employee has requested the Commissioner in the approved form to pay the amount to him or her.
@ref s 66A (src:1250-1253)
GIVEN `section 65AA covers the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a terminal medical condition within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 exists in relation to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has requested the Commissioner in the approved form to pay the amount to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must pay the shortfall component to an employee with a terminal medical condition` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 65AA covers the case` THEN NOTHING
           IF `a terminal medical condition within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 exists in relation to the employee` AND `the employee has requested the Commissioner in the approved form to pay the amount to the employee` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1254 | 67 Payment where employee deceased
-- src:1255 | Except in a case covered by section 65AA, if the employee has died, the Commissioner must pay the amount of the shortfall component to the legal personal representative of the employee.
@ref s 67 (src:1254-1255)
GIVEN `section 65AA covers the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee has died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner must pay the shortfall component to the legal personal representative of the employee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `section 65AA covers the case` THEN NOTHING
           IF `the employee has died` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 69, 69A and 71: overpayments`

-- src:1257 | (1) This section applies if the Commissioner pays an amount under a provision of this Part (other than paragraph 65(1)(c)) exceeding the amount properly payable under that provision.
@ref s 69(1), (2), (4) (src:1257-1257)
-- src:1258 | (2) The Commissioner may recover all or part of the excess from a person (the debtor) described in subsection (3) as a debt due by the debtor to the Commonwealth if the conditions specified in subsection (4) are met.
@ref s 69(1), (2), (4) (src:1258-1258)
-- src:1270 | (4) The conditions for recovery are that:
-- src:1271 | (a) the Commissioner gave the debtor a written notice of the proposed recovery that includes the amount to be recovered and an explanation of the operation of this section; and
-- src:1272 | (b) at least 28 days have passed since the notice was given; and
-- src:1273 | (c) the amount recovered is not more than the amount specified in the notice.
@ref s 69(1), (2), (4) (src:1270-1273)
GIVEN `the Commissioner gave the debtor a written notice of the proposed recovery that includes the amount to be recovered and an explanation of the operation of the section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the day of recovery` IS A DATE
      `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conditions for recovery are met` MEANS
        `the Commissioner gave the debtor a written notice of the proposed recovery that includes the amount to be recovered and an explanation of the operation of the section`
    AND `at least 28 days have passed since the notice was given` `the day the notice was given` `the day of recovery`
    AND `the amount recovered` AT MOST `the amount specified in the notice`

-- src:1259 | (3) The persons from whom the Commissioner may recover are as follows:
-- src:1260 | (a) the person to whom the payment was made;
-- src:1261 | (b) if:
-- src:1262 | (i) the person to whom the payment was made is a superannuation provider of a fund or RSA; and
-- src:1263 | (ii) there are one or more later transfers of the payment, or of amounts wholly or partly attributable to the payment, to one or more other funds or RSAs;
-- src:1264 | the superannuation provider for the fund or RSA that currently holds the payment or any of those attributable amounts;
-- src:1265 | (c) the benefitting employee for the payment (or the employee’s trustee) if:
-- src:1266 | (i) it is not possible to recover all or part of the excess from a person covered by paragraph (a) or (b); and
-- src:1267 | (ii) the benefitting employee (or the employee’s trustee) has received one or more benefits from a fund or RSA that are wholly or partly attributable to the payment.
-- src:1268 | Note 1: The kinds of persons covered by paragraph (a) include a benefitting employee, a superannuation provider, or the trustee of a benefitting employee who has died or who is under any legal or other disability.
-- src:1269 | Note 2: To find out who can be the benefitting employee’s trustee for paragraph (c), see section 6.
@ref s 69(3), (5) (src:1259-1269)
-- src:1274 | (5) Despite subsections (2) and (3):
-- src:1275 | (a) none of the excess can be recovered from a superannuation provider if none of the provider’s funds or RSAs currently hold the payment or any amount wholly or partly attributable to the payment; and
-- src:1276 | (b) the total amount recovered from a benefitting employee (or the employee’s trustee) because of paragraph (3)(c) must not exceed the total of the benefits received as described in that paragraph.
-- src:1277 | Note: The limit in paragraph (b) does not apply if the benefitting employee (or the employee’s trustee) is the person covered by paragraph (3)(a).
@ref s 69(3), (5) (src:1274-1277)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom the payment was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the superannuation provider for the fund or RSA that currently holds the payment or an amount attributable to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not possible to recover from a person covered by paragraph (a) or (b), and the benefitting employee or the employee's trustee has received benefits attributable to the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may recover the excess from the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person to whom the payment was made` OR `the person is the superannuation provider for the fund or RSA that currently holds the payment or an amount attributable to it` OR `it is not possible to recover from a person covered by paragraph (a) or (b), and the benefitting employee or the employee's trustee has received benefits attributable to the payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- 69(5)(b) and (7): from a benefitting employee under (3)(c) no more than the benefits received; across debtors no more than the excess in total.
-- src:1274 | (5) Despite subsections (2) and (3):
-- src:1275 | (a) none of the excess can be recovered from a superannuation provider if none of the provider’s funds or RSAs currently hold the payment or any amount wholly or partly attributable to the payment; and
-- src:1276 | (b) the total amount recovered from a benefitting employee (or the employee’s trustee) because of paragraph (3)(c) must not exceed the total of the benefits received as described in that paragraph.
-- src:1277 | Note: The limit in paragraph (b) does not apply if the benefitting employee (or the employee’s trustee) is the person covered by paragraph (3)(a).
@ref s 69(5), (7) (src:1274-1277)
-- src:1279 | (7) The total of the amounts recovered from different debtors in relation to the same excess must not be more than the excess.
@ref s 69(5), (7) (src:1279-1279)
GIVEN `the excess` IS A NUMBER
      `the total already recovered from other debtors for the same excess` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the benefits received, if recovery is from a benefitting employee or trustee under paragraph (3)(c)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that can still be recovered from a debtor` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the total of the benefits received, if recovery is from a benefitting employee or trustee under paragraph (3)(c)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN remaining
    WHEN JUST benefits THEN IF benefits LESS THAN remaining THEN benefits ELSE remaining
    WHERE
        remaining MEANS IF `the total already recovered from other debtors for the same excess` GREATER THAN `the excess` THEN 0 ELSE `the excess` MINUS `the total already recovered from other debtors for the same excess`

-- src:1278 | (6) The Commissioner may revoke a notice described in paragraph (4)(a).
@ref s 69(6), (8) (src:1278-1278)
-- src:1280 | (8) A notice described in paragraph (4)(a) is not a legislative instrument.
@ref s 69(6), (8) (src:1280-1280)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a notice of proposed recovery is a legislative instrument` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:1282 | (1) This section applies if:
-- src:1283 | (a) an amount credited by the Commissioner under paragraph 65(1)(c) of this Act to an account kept under the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995 exceeds the amount that should have been credited to the account; and
-- src:1284 | (b) the balance of the account is attributable, in whole or in part, to the credit.
@ref s 69A (src:1282-1284)
-- src:1285 | (2) The account is to be debited by the amount of the excess.
@ref s 69A (src:1285-1285)
-- src:1286 | (3) An amount equal to the excess is to be debited from the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account.
@ref s 69A (src:1286-1286)
GIVEN `the amount credited under paragraph 65(1)(c) to an account kept under the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that should have been credited` IS A NUMBER
      `the balance of the account is attributable in whole or in part to the credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount to be debited from the account and from the Superannuation Holding Accounts Special Account` MEANS
    IF `the amount credited under paragraph 65(1)(c) to an account kept under the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995` GREATER THAN `the amount that should have been credited` AND `the balance of the account is attributable in whole or in part to the credit`
    THEN JUST (`the amount credited under paragraph 65(1)(c) to an account kept under the Small Superannuation Accounts Act 1995` MINUS `the amount that should have been credited`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1287 | 71 Appropriation
-- src:1288 | Amounts that the Commissioner is required to pay under this Part are payable out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund, which is appropriated accordingly.
@ref s 71 (src:1287-1288)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`amounts the Commissioner is required to pay under Part 8 are payable out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` MEANS JUST TRUE

§ `Sections 72 and 73: partnerships and unincorporated associations`

-- src:1291 | (1) Subject to this section, this Act applies as if a partnership were a legal person.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1291-1291)
-- src:1292 | (2) An obligation that, apart from this subsection, would be imposed by this Act on a partnership is instead imposed on each partner, but may be discharged by any of the partners.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1292-1292)
-- src:1293 | (3) If, apart from this subsection, a liability to pay money would be imposed on a partnership by this Act, the liability is instead imposed on the partners jointly and severally.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1293-1293)
-- src:1294 | (4) If, because of subsection (1), a partnership would be taken to have committed an offence, the offence is instead taken to have been committed by each of the partners.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1294-1294)
-- src:1301 | (2) Subject to this section, this Act applies as if an association were a legal person.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1301-1301)
-- src:1302 | (3) An obligation that, apart from this subsection, would be imposed on an association is instead imposed on the officers of the association.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1302-1302)
-- src:1303 | (4) If, apart from this subsection, a liability to pay money would be imposed on an association by this Act, the liability is instead imposed on the members of the association jointly and severally.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1303-1303)
-- src:1304 | (5) If, because of subsection (2), an association would be taken to have committed an offence, the offence is instead taken to have been committed by each of the officers of the association.
@ref s 72(1) to (4), 73(2) to (5) (src:1304-1304)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the obligation or the liability or the offence of a partnership or association falls on the partners, members or officers` MEANS JUST TRUE

-- src:1295 | (5) In a prosecution for an offence taken to have been committed by a person because of subsection (4), it is a defence that the person:
-- src:1296 | (a) did not aid, abet, counsel or procure the act or omission constituting the offence; and
-- src:1297 | (b) was not in any way, by act or omission, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, the act or omission constituting the offence.
@ref s 72(5), 73(6) (src:1295-1297)
-- src:1305 | (6) In a prosecution for an offence taken to have been committed by a person by virtue of subsection (5), it is a defence that the person:
-- src:1306 | (a) did not aid, abet, counsel or procure the act or omission constituting the offence; and
-- src:1307 | (b) was not in any way, by act or omission, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, the act or omission constituting the offence.
@ref s 72(5), 73(6) (src:1305-1307)
GIVEN `the person did not aid, abet, counsel or procure the act or omission constituting the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was not in any way, by act or omission, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, the act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is a defence to an offence taken to have been committed by a partner or an officer` MEANS
    IF `the person did not aid, abet, counsel or procure the act or omission constituting the offence` AND `the person was not in any way, by act or omission, directly or indirectly, knowingly concerned in, or party to, the act or omission` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1300 | (1) In this section, association means an unincorporated association or body of persons (other than a partnership).
@ref s 73(1) (src:1300-1300)
GIVEN `it is an unincorporated association or body of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an association for the purposes of section 73` MEANS
    `it is an unincorporated association or body of persons` AND (NOT (`it is a partnership`))

§ `Section 74: the amnesty`

-- src:1311 | (1) An employer qualifies for an amnesty for the employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for a quarter if:
-- src:1312 | (a) during the period (the amnesty period) provided by subsection (3), the employer discloses to the Commissioner, in the approved form, information that:
-- src:1313 | (i) relates to the amount of the employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter; and
-- src:1314 | (ii) was not disclosed to the Commissioner before the amnesty period; and
-- src:1315 | (b) the amnesty period started after the end of the period of 28 days after the end of the quarter; and
-- src:1316 | (c) the Commissioner has not, at any time before the disclosure, informed the employer that the Commissioner is examining, or intends to examine, the employer’s compliance with an obligation to pay the superannuation guarantee charge for the quarter.
@ref s 74(1) (src:1311-1316)
GIVEN `the day the Royal Assent was received` IS A DATE
      `the day of the disclosure` IS A DATE
      `the disclosure is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the amount of the superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was not disclosed to the Commissioner before the amnesty period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the quarter` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner informed the employer before the disclosure that the Commissioner is, or intends to be, looking into the employer's compliance with an obligation to pay the charge for the quarter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an employer qualifies for an amnesty for the shortfall for a quarter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a disclosure is made during the amnesty period` `the day the Royal Assent was received` `the day of the disclosure`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST during THEN
        JUST (    during
              AND `the disclosure is in the approved form`
              AND `the information relates to the amount of the superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter`
              AND `the information was not disclosed to the Commissioner before the amnesty period`
              AND `the amnesty period started after the end of the 28 days after the quarter` `the last day of the quarter`
              AND (NOT (`the Commissioner informed the employer before the disclosure that the Commissioner is, or intends to be, looking into the employer's compliance with an obligation to pay the charge for the quarter`)))

-- src:1317 | (2) However, if the employer would have a superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter even if the information in the disclosure were not taken into account, the employer qualifies for an amnesty for the shortfall only to the extent of the increase in the shortfall as a result of taking the information into account.
@ref s 74(2) (src:1317-1317)
GIVEN `the shortfall for the quarter taking the information into account` IS A NUMBER
      `the shortfall for the quarter not taking the information into account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shortfall for which the employer qualifies for the amnesty` MEANS
    IF `the shortfall for the quarter not taking the information into account` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the shortfall for the quarter taking the information into account` MINUS `the shortfall for the quarter not taking the information into account`
    ELSE `the shortfall for the quarter taking the information into account`

-- src:1322 | (4) The employer ceases to qualify, and is taken never to have qualified, for the amnesty for the employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter if the Commissioner notifies the employer under subsection (5).
@ref s 74(4) to (6) (src:1322-1322)
-- src:1323 | (5) The Commissioner may notify the employer in writing that the employer has ceased to qualify, and is taken never to have qualified, for that amnesty if:
-- src:1324 | (a) the employer:
-- src:1325 | (i) has not, on or before the day on which superannuation guarantee charge on the employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter became payable, paid that superannuation guarantee charge; and
-- src:1326 | (ii) has not, at any time, entered into an arrangement with the Commissioner that includes the payment of that superannuation guarantee charge; or
-- src:1327 | (b) the employer has entered into such an arrangement, but has failed to comply with it.
@ref s 74(4) to (6) (src:1323-1327)
-- src:1328 | (6) For the purposes of subparagraph (5)(a)(i), a payment under this Act of an amount equal to the amount of the superannuation guarantee charge mentioned in that subparagraph is taken to be a payment of that charge whether or not the Commissioner applies the payment to satisfy the employer’s liability to pay that charge.
@ref s 74(4) to (6) (src:1328-1328)
GIVEN `the employer has paid the charge on or before the day on which it became payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has at some time entered into an arrangement with the Commissioner that includes payment of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has failed to comply with that arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Commissioner may notify the employer that it has ceased to qualify for the amnesty` MEANS
    IF ((NOT (`the employer has paid the charge on or before the day on which it became payable`)) AND (NOT (`the employer has at some time entered into an arrangement with the Commissioner that includes payment of the charge`)))
       OR (`the employer has at some time entered into an arrangement with the Commissioner that includes payment of the charge` AND `the employer has failed to comply with that arrangement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1322 | (4) The employer ceases to qualify, and is taken never to have qualified, for the amnesty for the employer’s superannuation guarantee shortfall for the quarter if the Commissioner notifies the employer under subsection (5).
@ref s 74(4) (src:1322-1322)
GIVEN `the Commissioner has notified the employer under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer ceases to qualify, and is taken never to have qualified, for the amnesty` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has notified the employer under subsection (5)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 79: records`

-- src:1330 | (1) An employer must keep records that record and explain all transactions and other acts engaged in by the employer, or required to be engaged in by the employer, under this Act.
-- src:1331 | Note: There is an administrative penalty if you do not keep or retain records as required by this section: see section 288-25 in Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953.
@ref s 79(1) to (3) (src:1330-1331)
-- src:1332 | (2) The records must include any documents relevant to working out:
-- src:1333 | (a) whether the employer has a superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day; and
-- src:1334 | (b) the amount of such a shortfall.
@ref s 79(1) to (3) (src:1332-1334)
-- src:1335 | (3) The records must be kept:
-- src:1336 | (a) in writing in the English language or so as to enable the records to be readily accessible and convertible into writing in the English language; and
-- src:1337 | (b) so that the employer’s liability under this Act can be readily ascertained.
@ref s 79(1) to (3) (src:1335-1337)
GIVEN `the records record and explain all transactions and other acts engaged in or required to be engaged in by the employer under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records include any documents relevant to working out whether the employer has a shortfall for a QE day and its amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are kept in writing in the English language or so as to be readily accessible and convertible into it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are kept so that the liability of the employer under the Act can be readily ascertained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the employer keeps the records section 79 requires` MEANS
        `the records record and explain all transactions and other acts engaged in or required to be engaged in by the employer under the Act`
    AND `the records include any documents relevant to working out whether the employer has a shortfall for a QE day and its amount`
    AND `the records are kept in writing in the English language or so as to be readily accessible and convertible into it`
    AND `the records are kept so that the liability of the employer under the Act can be readily ascertained`

-- src:1338 | (4) An employer who has possession of any records kept or obtained under or for the purposes of this Act must retain them until the end of 5 years after those records were prepared or obtained, or the completion of the transactions or acts to which those records relate, whichever is later.
@ref s 79(4), (5) (src:1338-1338)
-- src:1339 | (5) Nothing in this section requires an employer to retain records if:
-- src:1340 | (a) the Commissioner has notified the employer that the retention of the records is not required; or
-- src:1341 | (b) the employer is a company that has gone into liquidation and been finally dissolved.
-- src:1342 | Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsection (5), see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.
@ref s 79(4), (5) (src:1339-1342)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the day the records were prepared or obtained` IS A DATE
      `the day the transactions or acts were completed` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner has notified the employer that the retention of the records is not required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is a company that has gone into liquidation and been finally dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer must retain the records on the day` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has notified the employer that the retention of the records is not required` OR `the employer is a company that has gone into liquidation and been finally dissolved`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `the retention period has not yet ended` `the day asked about` `the day the records were prepared or obtained` `the day the transactions or acts were completed`

-- src:1343 | (6) An employer who contravenes this section commits an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 30 penalty units.
-- src:1344 | Note: See section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914 for the current value of a penalty unit.
@ref s 79(6), (6A), (7) (src:1343-1344)
-- src:1345 | (6A) Subsection (6) does not apply to the extent that the person has a reasonable excuse.
-- src:1346 | Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matters in subsection (6A), see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.
@ref s 79(6), (6A), (7) (src:1345-1346)
-- src:1347 | (7) An offence under this section is an offence of strict liability.
-- src:1348 | Note: For strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.
@ref s 79(6), (6A), (7) (src:1347-1348)
GIVEN `the employer contravenes section 79` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the employer commits an offence against section 79` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`the employer contravenes section 79`) THEN NOTHING
           IF `the person has a reasonable excuse` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1343 | (6) An employer who contravenes this section commits an offence punishable on conviction by a fine not exceeding 30 penalty units.
-- src:1344 | Note: See section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914 for the current value of a penalty unit.
@ref s 79(6) (src:1343-1344)
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest fine for an offence against section 79` MEANS 30 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`

-- src:1353 | and, in particular, may make regulations prescribing penalties not exceeding a fine of 5 penalty units for offences against the regulations.
@ref s 80 (src:1353-1353)
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest fine the regulations may prescribe for an offence against the regulations` MEANS 5 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`
